          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "ShowInitActions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SHOWINITACTIONS",
          "id": "1764964858996",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764964858997_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Inputs**  \n- **Query Response:** `{{$context.$variables.responseDetails}}`  \n- **Action Details :** `{{$context.$variables.actionDetails}}`\n- **Communication Details:** `{{$context.$variables.communicationDetails}}`\n\n---\n\n### **Tasks**\n1. **Using only from available Action Details (actionCode, actionCondition) aligned with User Request, Inbound Context Details and the Query Response:**  \n   - Provide priority actionable insights (ranked by priority, relevance) in below sample format\n{\n  \"title\": \"Suggestion: turn off lights\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"No one was detected in the house, suggest you turn off the lights.\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Turn Off Lights\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"sendAgentCmd\\\",  \\\"<payload>\\\")\",\n  \"priority\":\"false\"\n}\n - <payload> format is `{\"actionCode\": \"<actionCode>\"}`\n - Include actions along with widgets only if relevant else show separately as action items. \n - consider actions based on actionCondition  \n - use actionCode, actionTitle, actionText, actionPurpose available only from the **Action Details**\n - followUpCommand must include \"sendAgentCmd\"\n\n\n3)   analyze the user's request and select all commConditions that match from **Communication Details:**. \nFor each matching commCondition, generate all relevant low-priority actionable communication suggestions using the commType (\"email\" or \"text\") and the provided JSON schema. \nRank these communications below major priority actions.\nAlways generate minimum of 2 communication suggestions.\n\nFor email communications:\n- Do not fabricate recipients; leave the \"email\" param empty if unknown.\n- Generate rich text content (use HTML markers if appropriate), including a salutation, one-sentence meeting/alert summary, purpose/agenda as per commPrompt, \nand a closing signed by {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}}.\n\nFor text communications:\n- Structure the content as a clear, concise alert aligning with the commPurpose and commPrompt.\n\nWrap each communication suggestion in `<oraComms>...</oraComms>` tags.\n\n**Email JSON structure**:\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"<title based on commPurpose or commCode>\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"<one-line description using commPurpose>\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Send email\",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n  \"content\": \"<full email body derived from commPrompt; include salutation, closing and sign with {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}}>\",\n  \"params\": [\n    { \"id\": \"email\", \"title\": \"email address\", \"defaultValue\": \"\" },\n    { \"id\": \"subject\", \"title\": \"email subject\", \"defaultValue\": \"<short subject from commPurpose or commPrompt>\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Text JSON structure**:\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"<title based on commPurpose or commCode>\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"<one-line description using commPurpose>\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Alert\",\n  \"type\": \"text\",\n  \"content\": \"<full alert text derived from commPurpose or commPrompt>\",\n  \"params\": [\n    { \"id\": \"<id>\", \"title\": \"<short subject from commPurpose or commPrompt>\", \"defaultValue\": \"<short subject from commPurpose or commPrompt>\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Instructions**:\n- Always output all relevant communication suggestions based on the available commCondition and commType, ranked below any primary actions.\n- Use available fields from Communication Details only; do not invent additional data or recipients.\n- Output each individual suggestion as:\n  ```\n  <oraComms>\n    { ...communication JSON... }\n  </oraComms>\n  ```\n\n**Example output**:\n```\n<oraComms>\n  { ...communication JSON... }\n</oraComms>\n<oraComms>\n  { ...communication JSON... }\n</oraComms>\n```\n```\n\n---\n---\n\n**User Request:**  \nCurrent prompt: `{{$context.$variables.userPrompt}}`  \nChat history: `{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}`"
            }
          ],
