          "code": "GENERATEINITCOMMUNICATION",
          "id": "1764963747386",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764963747389_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**Date Interpretation Rules** `{{$context.$variables.DateInterpretationRules}}`\n**Current Date** `{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}`\n**Response Data** :  `{{$context.$variables.responseDetails}}`\n\nGenerate below communications\n#Communication-1\n## CONTEXT\nResponse Data contains team details including hire dates.\nYou are assisting a manager in drafting email to introduce new hires to team (with DateStart in past one month from current date).\nUsing Date Interpretation Rules, identify all team members whose DateStart is within the last month. Perform precise date comparison, never estimate. For reference: If today’s date is 2026-04-12, include any employees with DateStart between 2026-03-12 and 2026-04-12.\n- EffectiveStartDate and DateStart are two distinct entities and should not be used interchangeably\n\nDO NOT show email communication when there are no new hires identified.\n\n## TASKS\n- Generate a neat, structured report to email it, using well-formatted and indented text, and use HTML <b> tags only for headers and sub-headers.\n\n## EMAIL METADATA\n{\n  \"title\": \"New Hires introduction\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"New Hires introduction to the team\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Email New Hires introduction\",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n   \"content\" : \"generate email content using sample email structure given below with below one table\n    Using  Date Interpretation Rules identify employees who joined the company within the past month. \n    1) only for employees whose DateStart is with last one month, generate HTML table showing Employee Name, Job, Department, Date Start. \n  \n  \",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"email\",\n      \"title\": \"email address\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"subject\",\n      \"title\": \"New Hires introduction\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n## SAMPLE EMAIL STRUCTURE\n<p>Hi Team,</p>\n<p> <!-- 2-3 sentences introducing new team members  --> </p>\n<ul>\n  <!-- Add New joineers in HTML table  -->\n</ul>\n<br/>\n<br/>\nBest Regards<br/>\n{{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}}<br/>\n\n\n#Communication-2\nResponse data provided with employment data below, where displayName represents the employee name:\n\nProduce one \"text\" communication suggestion with the following:\n title: Work Anniversaries\n description: one sentence on what you would show in alert (summary)\n actionText: Alert\n content: Include the following information in the communication content\n      Employees details (name, job, department name, work anniversary date of current year based on DateStart)\nContent presentation :- Present details in list output sorted based on work anniversary date ascending.\n\n\n#Communication-3\n## CONTEXT\nResponse data provided with employment, talent and compensation details, where displayName represents the employee name:\nYou are assisting a manager in drafting email to generate summary of team talent and compensation details.\n\n## TASKS\n- Generate a neat, structured report to email it, using well-formatted and indented text or tabular output, and use HTML <b> tags only for headers and sub-headers.\n\n## EMAIL METADATA\n{\n  \"title\": \"Team Review Reminder\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Summary of team talent and compensation to review\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Team Talent and Compensation Review \",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n  \"content\" : \"generate email content using sample email structure given below with below two tables\n  1) only for employees whose Risk of Loss and Impact of Loss are High, generate HTML table showing Employee Name, Job, Performance Rating, Impact of Loss and Risk of Loss. \n  2) only for employees whose compa-ratio is below 100, generate HTML table showing Employee Name, Job, Current Salary, Salary Range, Compa-Ratio, Performance Rating\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"email\",\n      \"title\": \"email address\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"subject\",\n      \"title\": \"Talent and Compensation Review\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n## SAMPLE EMAIL STRUCTURE\n<p>Hi {{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}},</p>\n<p>Reminder to review the talent and compensation details of team</p>\n<h3>High Risk Employees</h3>\n<ul>\n  <!-- Add High Risk Employees HTML table  -->\n</ul>\n<h3>Low Salary Employees</h3>\n<ul>\n  <!-- Add Low Salary Employees HTML table  -->\n</ul>\n<br/>\n<br/>\nBest Regards<br/>\n\n\n\n# CONSTRAINTS\n- Base recommendations only on provided evidence."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
